  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat on 2026-11-16:\n\n> bug, we decide to pput the work envelope on the \"floor\" of the grid.. The model still loads halv way down, thru the floor. also the \"fixtures\" generation, moves down under the floor.. The should move the move the model and stock with the fixture to the \"floor\" of the workspace when created. Also model should drop back down when removed..  Basis is that things happen on the floor of the work envelope thus the grid..\n\nWhat happens:\n\n- The work envelope stands on the grid (the floor). A loaded model does not: half of the model is below the floor.\n- A generated fixture goes below the floor.\n\nExpected:\n\n- The floor of the work envelope is the grid. All bodies stand on it.\n- A loaded model stands on the floor.\n- When a fixture is created, the fixture stands on the floor. The model and the stock move up with it and stand on the fixture.\n- When the fixture is removed, the model and the stock go back down to the floor.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Each placement change that the document stores is an undoable command (AGENTS.md \"Everything Is a Command\"). Undo restores the earlier position.\n- The WCS comes from the setup. A move of the model with its stock and fixture must not change the posted coordinates of an existing program. If it can change them, the work is under the safety floor and the PR says so.\n- Carried stock, the collision checks and the simulation must read the same positions as the viewport shows.\n- Check the lathe arrangement also: its envelope lies along the spindle axis.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins that a loaded model has its lowest point on the floor of the work envelope.\n- A test pins that a created fixture stands on the floor, and that the model and the stock stand on the fixture.\n- A test pins that the model and the stock return to the floor when the fixture is removed, and that undo and redo restore each state.\n- A test pins that the posted G-code of an existing project does not change.\n",
